1
00:00:00,000 --> 00:00:03,344
Chapter ten — the Code lens.

2
00:00:03,404 --> 00:00:15,038
Four lenses model the system you intend.
This one reads the system you actually wrote.

3
00:00:15,098 --> 00:00:23,749
Point it at a repository
and it indexes the source.

4
00:00:23,809 --> 00:00:33,258
Symbols, files and calls — the call
graph of the codebase, not a folder tree.

5
00:00:33,318 --> 00:00:37,956
Browse walks the files.

6
00:00:38,016 --> 00:00:58,024
Search by symbol, or switch to
text and search the source itself.

7
00:00:58,084 --> 00:01:07,528
Pick a symbol and you get its call
graph: what calls it, and what it calls.

8
00:01:07,588 --> 00:01:20,415
Depth one is the neighbours. Two and
three follow the blast radius out.

9
00:01:20,475 --> 00:01:36,911
Shape is the kind of symbol. Colour is
its scope. The legend is on the graph.

10
00:01:36,971 --> 00:01:53,000
Hide local helpers strips the
noise so the real structure shows.

11
00:01:53,060 --> 00:02:02,505
Tests reads your test run — pass,
fail and how long each one took.

12
00:02:02,565 --> 00:02:17,005
Failures first, then the slowest, then by
file. Real results, not a coverage badge.

13
00:02:17,065 --> 00:02:35,627
Insights is what the index found: dead code,
cycles, and the hubs where change is risky.

14
00:02:35,687 --> 00:02:46,629
Load a test profile and the graph gets a
heat overlay — where the time actually went.

15
00:02:46,689 --> 00:02:52,693
The architecture is the intent.
The code lens is the evidence.
